                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00707         *************************
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00708         * Level 2 flags used for bytes in the memory block map at D.BlkMap
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00709         * and for bytes in the system memory map at D.SysMem.
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00710         * A value of 0 indicates an unused/unassigned block.
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00711         * In the code, block assignment often involves incrementing a value
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00712         * from 0 to 1 rather than explict use of RAMinUse.
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00713         *
0112                  (    ../defs/os9.d):00714         NotRAM              EQU       %10000000           Block Not RAM flag
0112                  (    ../defs/os9.d):00715         VidRAM              EQU       %00000100           Block is being used as Video RAM
0112                  (    ../defs/os9.d):00716         ModBlock            EQU       %00000010           Module in Block
0112                  (    ../defs/os9.d):00717         RAMinUse            EQU       %00000001           RAM Block in use flag
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00718         *
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00719         * Service Dispatch Table special entries
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00720         *
0112                  (    ../defs/os9.d):00721         IOEntry             EQU       254
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00722         
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00723                             ENDC
