                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00861         *
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00862         * Attribute Flags
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00863         *
     0080             (    ../defs/os9.d):00864         ReEnt               EQU       %10000000           Re-Entrant Module
     0040             (    ../defs/os9.d):00865         ModProt             EQU       %01000000           Gimix Module protect bit (0=protected, 1=write enable)
     0020             (    ../defs/os9.d):00866         ModNat              EQU       %00100000           6309 native mode attribute
     0040             (    ../defs/os9.d):00867         BufWrits            EQU       ModProt             SCF buffered read supported (Coco only at this point)
     0010             (    ../defs/os9.d):00868         BufReads            EQU       %00010000           SCF buffered write supported (Coco only at this point)
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00869         * LCB - propose we add Buffered Read/Buffered Write attribute bits for Coco (in descriptors and
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00870         *   drivers for SCF), with one of them replacing ModProt. SCF would check Read/ReadLn and Write/WritLn
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00871         *   calls, and if both the driver and descriptor have the appropriate bit set, it would do buffered 32
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00872         *   byte (for now) reads/writes like the Grfdrv write call does now, for all bytes that are ASCII >$1F
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00873         *   (ie non-control chars, which need special processing)
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00874         
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00875         
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00876         ********************
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00877         * Device Type Values
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00878         *
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00879         * These values define various classes of devices, which are
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00880         * managed by a file manager module.  The Device Type is embedded
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00881         * in a device's device descriptor.
                      (    ../defs/os9.d):00882         *
     0000             (    ../defs/os9.d):00883         DT.SCF              EQU       0                   Sequential Character File Manager
     0001             (    ../defs/os9.d):00884         DT.RBF              EQU       1                   Random Block File Manager
     0002             (    ../defs/os9.d):00885         DT.Pipe             EQU       2                   Pipe File Manager
     0003             (    ../defs/os9.d):00886         DT.SBF              EQU       3                   Sequential Block File Manager
     0004             (    ../defs/os9.d):00887         DT.NFM              EQU       4                   Network File Manager
     0005             (    ../defs/os9.d):00888         DT.CDFM             EQU       5                   CD-ROM File Manager
     0006             (    ../defs/os9.d):00889         DT.RFM              EQU       6                   Remote File Manager
